\title{Discrete and Indiscrete Topologies}
\taxon{Definition}
\p{
    Let #{X} be a set. The \strong{discrete topology} on #{X} is the power set
    #{\mathcal{P}(X)}, so every subset is open. The \strong{indiscrete
    topology} is #{\{\varnothing,X\}}, so only the two sets required by the
    topology axioms are open.
}
\p{
    These are respectively the [finest and coarsest](def-005X) topologies on
    the fixed underlying set #{X}.
}
